\begin_layout Standard
A zero ring is any singleton ring with matching additive and multiplicative identities as the sole element of the ring.
 All zero rings are isomorphic to each other,
 thus referred to as 
\emph on
the
\emph default
 zero ring.
 Integral domains and fields require 
\begin_inset Formula $0\ne1$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

