\begin_layout Standard
A module 
\begin_inset Formula $M$
\end_inset

 over 
\begin_inset Formula $R$
\end_inset

 is 
\emph on
finite free
\emph default
 if it has a finite ordered basis 
\begin_inset Formula $E=(\boldsymbol{e}_{1},\ldots,\boldsymbol{e}_{n})$
\end_inset

:
 
\begin_inset Formula $\forall\boldsymbol{x}\in M$
\end_inset

,
 
\begin_inset Formula $\exists!x_{1},\ldots,x_{n}\in R$
\end_inset

,
 such that
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\boldsymbol{x}=\sum\nolimits^{n}_{i=1}x_{i}\boldsymbol{e}_{i}\quad\longleftrightarrow\quad(x_{1},\ldots,x_{n})\in R^{n},
\]

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $R^{n}$
\end_inset

 is a module over 
\begin_inset Formula $R$
\end_inset

,
 therefore this coordinate correspondence is a module isomorphism.
 A general module need not have a basis.
\end_layout

